      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.49,
      "end": 1.9,
      "text": "Hey, how's your week going?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 7.88,
      "end": 14.2,
      "text": "There's no single rule anymore. Many couples pay most of it themselves, and parents contribute what they can or want to."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.38,
      "end": 26.06,
      "text": "That's common. You could gently ask if they'd like to help with something specific, like the rehearsal dinner or the flowers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 28.63,
      "end": 33.84,
      "text": "Not if you frame it as an invitation, not a bill. Some parents love having one thing that's theirs."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 36.89,
      "end": 42.64,
      "text": "Then you plan with what you have. And try not to compare, it can create tension that lasts longer than the wedding."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 50.43,
      "end": 53.69,
      "text": "Good instinct. It usually goes better coming from their own kid."
    }
